### Invalid test inputs

The same fixture backs all three failures. It is topologically valid but assembles successfully on the initial pass, so it never produces a `SameCornerDistinctBoundaryClaim` and never enters structural repair.

- `WholeComplexParallelRouteRepairCompletesWithinOneGlobalLedger`
- `ZeroStructuralBudgetFailsBeforeCandidateExpansion`
- `OneCandidateBudgetIsExactAndDoesNotRecurse`

`StructuralRepairLedgerIsPatchOrderInvariant` also passes vacuously with zero attempts. Replace the fixture with an authoritative same-corner input and assert that precondition before budget or order checks. Do not weaken production behavior or force repair on an already successful complex.

